Z||000000||kornholio||09-21-1999||05:58 PM||||Are the alternators for the Fiero made for the Fiero only?  I went to the wreckers and they gave me a Pontiac 6000 alternator.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Dan||09-21-1999||08:32 PM|||| Many alternators from many several years from practically all gm products will interchange. Main difference of gm alternators is the pulley configerations.||||reg||1
Z||000002||kornholio||09-21-1999||09:31 PM||||Do all alternators come with a voltage regulator?  How do I know if the one I bought came with one?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||09-21-1999||10:34 PM||||If your alternator came off of a pont. 6000 it has the regulator built in. GM cars since about 1974 have had internal regulators. Make sure that you have the right type alternator though- later model "small case" alterators will not have the right connectors to fit our cars.||||reg||3
